Z||000003||turbo86se||06-02-2001||03:11 PM||||I'm putting that down on my calender, sounds like a real nice day trip.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||LZeitgeist||06-02-2001||06:16 PM||||Formula88 - June 14th is a Thursday... July 14th is a Saturday.<P>Bob and Harry and I have only been tossing around either June 30th, or July 14th, as far as I know... <P>I apologize if I happened to mis-speak in one of our conversations, but yes, it's July 14th. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||LZeitgeist||06-02-2001||06:44 PM||||Dinner will be at the Weeping Radish Bavarian Restaurant and Brewpub... they have a full menu of traditional German food, and *incredible* beer for those of us who like that sort of thing.<P>I will call next weekend to try and get them to reserve the Loft for our group to gather and dine in, but I'll need to get a good head count to give them an idea of how many to expect. Please post here in this thread as to whether or not you are going to want to join us for dinner Saturday evening.<P>We also need to decide on a time. My first thought would be 4:00pm... that will give us two-and-a-half hours baking our brains in the sun at the Wright Memorial, and about a half-hour to get to the Radish (it's only about 15 minutes away, but you know this group is gonna be like herdin' cats... &lt;grin&gt; )... that will also give the people who are driving back home instead of staying in town for the night a little extra time to get home.  Or, would people prefer 5:00pm?<P>The easiest thing to do is place your vote for the time in with your message here saying you'd like to be included in dinner. Post your vote and yea/nay here in this thread <B>no later than Friday, June 8th at midnight</B>, and I will call the Radish this coming weekend, June 9th. <P>Disclaimer: Dinner/drinks/etc. are to be paid by each individual... the group is not providing dinner, just in case I may have not been clear about that (just trying to avoid miscommunications)... also, if you plan on indulging in the Radish's wonderful German beer, it is suggested that plans be made to stay overnight. The Duke of Dare is within a few blocks walking distance from the Radish in Manteo, and the Elizabethan Inn is also available a few blocks further away (not really walking distance, but still relatively close). Staying in Manteo (as opposed to Kitty Hawk/Nags Head/Kill Devil Hills) means you don't pay beach hotel prices...||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroHarry||06-02-2001||10:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B><BR>I will call next weekend to try and get them to reserve the Loft for our group to gather and dine in, but I'll need to get a good head count to give them an idea of how many to expect. Please post here in this thread as to whether or not you are going to want to join us for dinner Saturday evening.<P>LZ You are the man <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I would say that 4 or 5 PM is just fine but you never know when you get a bunch of Fieros together, they can really talk <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>"Yes" to dinner... <BR><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||1
